<title>USA: Rhone-Poulenc Rorer gets ALS drug okays.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer gets ALS drug okays.</headline>
<dateline>COLLEGEVILLE, Pa. 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer Inc said Thursday that it has received marketing clearance in Colombia, Mexico, Peru, Uruguay and Israel for Rilutek Tablets for the treatment of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis (ALS), a fatal neurodegenerative disease also known as Lou Gehrig's disease.</p>
<p>According to Rhone Rorer, Rilutek is the first drug in the world to be made available for the treatment of ALS, a disease that is characterized by progressive muscle weakening and paralysis.</p>
